<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">YHWH</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yahweh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">YHWH, conventionally rendered as Yahweh, is the name of the God of Israel in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>. The Assyrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> of the population of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> had consequences for Jewish religious thought. The experience of exile encouraged a reconceptualisation of YHWH as a universal deity not bound to a specific territory, contributing to the development of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monotheism">monotheism</a>.</p></div>
